WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.868 --> 00:00:01.868
-Thank you so much.

00:00:01.868 --> 00:00:03.067
Welcome to "The Tonight Show."

00:00:03.067 --> 00:00:04.534
Thank you for being here.
-Thanks for having me.

00:00:04.534 --> 00:00:09.234
-You are my -- You are my "FIFA"
player when I play video games.

00:00:09.234 --> 00:00:10.467
-You play "FIFA"?
[ Laughter ]

00:00:10.467 --> 00:00:11.701
-I play you.
Yeah, you're my guy.

00:00:11.701 --> 00:00:13.033
-Okay.
-So, I just want to say

00:00:13.033 --> 00:00:15.100
thank you for all the wins.
-Any goal -- Any goals?

00:00:15.100 --> 00:00:16.300
-Yeah, fantastic.
Oh, are you kidding me?

00:00:16.300 --> 00:00:17.467
Yeah.
"Kane!"

00:00:17.467 --> 00:00:18.968
I get it all the time, yeah.
That's --

00:00:18.968 --> 00:00:21.701
You're one of the top
soccer players in the world,

00:00:21.701 --> 00:00:24.567
you're captain
of the England national team.

00:00:24.567 --> 00:00:27.534
You've won countless awards.
There's an exhibit about you

00:00:27.534 --> 00:00:29.601
at the Museum of London
right now.

00:00:29.601 --> 00:00:32.300
-That's right, yeah.
-When you were a kid, did, like,

00:00:32.300 --> 00:00:35.667
your coaches think like,
"Oh, this -- this kid, Harry,

00:00:35.667 --> 00:00:37.000
is gonna be a superstar?"

00:00:37.000 --> 00:00:38.834
-No, I don't think so.
I don't think --

00:00:38.834 --> 00:00:40.968
I mean,
I was good when I was younger,

00:00:40.968 --> 00:00:42.934
but I don't think I was
the best player on the team.

00:00:42.934 --> 00:00:44.367
And I really had
to kind of work hard

00:00:44.367 --> 00:00:46.033
to kind of prove people wrong.

00:00:46.033 --> 00:00:48.734
But I think that's what made me
kind of who I am today

00:00:48.734 --> 00:00:50.334
and got me to the level
I got to,

00:00:50.334 --> 00:00:53.968
'cause that kind of self-belief,
that drive, that determination.

00:00:53.968 --> 00:00:55.734
And that's kind of what the
museum's there, to kind of --

00:00:55.734 --> 00:00:57.801
kids can go and look at that
and see my journey,

00:00:57.801 --> 00:01:01.033
and hopefully, one day, they can
aspire to be where I am.

00:01:01.033 --> 00:01:04.300
-What gets you inspired?
What -- what --

00:01:04.300 --> 00:01:06.000
What do you watch,
or what do you read,

00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:07.834
where you go like,
"Oh, that's inspires me"?

00:01:07.834 --> 00:01:11.534
-Yeah, I mean, one thing
that did inspire me kind of

00:01:11.534 --> 00:01:14.501
growing up was actually
a Tom Brady documentary.

00:01:14.501 --> 00:01:17.934
I was -- I was away
at another club, on loan,

00:01:17.934 --> 00:01:19.767
and kind of I wasn't
getting the team,

00:01:19.767 --> 00:01:22.501
and it was kind of that period
in my -- I was 18 years old --

00:01:22.501 --> 00:01:24.400
it was like,
"If I can't play here,

00:01:24.400 --> 00:01:27.667
how can I play for my team?"
Tottenham, at the time.

00:01:27.667 --> 00:01:30.367
Come across this documentary
on YouTube.

00:01:30.367 --> 00:01:32.334
It was -- I think it was called
"The Brady 6."

00:01:32.334 --> 00:01:34.934
It was kind of about how he got
picked in the 6th round,

00:01:34.934 --> 00:01:37.200
and then become who he become,

00:01:37.200 --> 00:01:38.968
one of the greatest
sportsmen ever.

00:01:38.968 --> 00:01:41.934
And it just gave me a real
belief that it was possible

00:01:41.934 --> 00:01:44.601
for me to go on and kind of
have that -- have that career.

00:01:44.601 --> 00:01:48.300
And, yeah, thankfully,
I was able to do that.

00:01:48.300 --> 00:01:50.167
-It's a boost, yeah.
And you -- you've gotten to be

00:01:50.167 --> 00:01:51.734
friends with Tom Brady now,
right?

00:01:51.734 --> 00:01:53.167
-Yeah, I mean, we --
we've got in touch.

00:01:53.167 --> 00:01:55.801
I mean, I was kind of following
him on Instagram,

00:01:55.801 --> 00:01:57.534
and he kind of commented
on one of my --

00:01:57.534 --> 00:01:59.901
my pictures when I --
-You slid into his DMs?

00:01:59.901 --> 00:02:02.100
[ Laughter ]

00:02:02.100 --> 00:02:04.601
-I slid into his DMs and --

00:02:04.601 --> 00:02:06.667
No, he was a great guy.
We kind of got talking.

00:02:06.667 --> 00:02:08.934
I kind of --
I'm -- I'm an NFL fan,

00:02:08.934 --> 00:02:10.267
so I was kind of wishing him
luck for --

00:02:10.267 --> 00:02:11.701
for the season and stuff.

00:02:11.701 --> 00:02:14.501
And, yeah, just kind of grew a
relationship from there, really.

00:02:14.501 --> 00:02:18.133
-Did you know that he was gonna
come out of retirement?

00:02:18.133 --> 00:02:20.000
-I mean, I wasn't 100% sure.

00:02:20.000 --> 00:02:22.100
He actually come to --
to a game,

00:02:22.100 --> 00:02:25.167
one of our games in the U.K.
about two months ago.

00:02:25.167 --> 00:02:26.767
It was actually the day before
he announced

00:02:26.767 --> 00:02:28.968
he was coming back to play.

00:02:28.968 --> 00:02:30.601
And I asked him, I was like,
"Oh, how you getting on?

00:02:30.601 --> 00:02:32.067
How's retirement treating you?"

00:02:32.067 --> 00:02:36.300
And his face just was like, "Mm,
I'm not sure if I'm ready yet."

00:02:36.300 --> 00:02:39.033
So, I mean, he didn't, like,
say he wasn't --

00:02:39.033 --> 00:02:40.133
-Yeah, you were like,
"Wait a second.

00:02:40.133 --> 00:02:41.400
Did he just say
what I think he did?"

00:02:41.400 --> 00:02:44.167
-Yeah, pretty much.
So, I mean, yeah.

00:02:44.167 --> 00:02:46.467
So, next day, he announced it,
which was --

00:02:46.467 --> 00:02:47.501
I thought it was great,
you know?

00:02:47.501 --> 00:02:49.734
It's great.
I love watching him.

00:02:49.734 --> 00:02:51.033
-Yeah.
-And it's great for the sport.

00:02:51.033 --> 00:02:55.667
-If ever emergency need be,
and they need a kicker

00:02:55.667 --> 00:02:58.467
for the Buccaneers,
or the New York Giants

00:02:58.467 --> 00:02:59.901
or the Jets...
-Yeah.

00:02:59.901 --> 00:03:01.367
-...could you step in?

00:03:01.367 --> 00:03:04.300
Would you be a good kicker?
Could you kick field goals?

00:03:04.300 --> 00:03:06.200
-I mean, I feel like I could.

00:03:06.200 --> 00:03:07.968
I'd put myself up there,
for sure.

00:03:07.968 --> 00:03:10.434
-Yeah.
We're -- like to --

00:03:10.434 --> 00:03:13.100
I don't have any tie-in
with any organization,

00:03:13.100 --> 00:03:15.033
but we would love to welcome you
to New York.

00:03:15.033 --> 00:03:18.000
[ Laughter ]
Play for either one.

00:03:18.000 --> 00:03:20.801
But you actually
brought us a video

00:03:20.801 --> 00:03:23.467
of you actually making
a 50-yard field goal?

00:03:23.467 --> 00:03:25.167
-Yeah, this is in New York,
as well, yeah.

00:03:25.167 --> 00:03:26.300
-How did you end up doing this?

00:03:26.300 --> 00:03:28.667
-This was on preseason
with our team,

00:03:28.667 --> 00:03:31.234
and we kind of -- I was doing
something with the Giants.

00:03:31.234 --> 00:03:34.267
And, yeah, kind of just
kicking some field goals

00:03:34.267 --> 00:03:35.901
and knocked a few in, yeah.

00:03:35.901 --> 00:03:39.434
-Let's take a look at this.

00:03:39.434 --> 00:03:40.868
Yes!

00:03:40.868 --> 00:03:45.200
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:45.200 --> 00:03:47.367
You booted it!
Oh, my gosh.

00:03:47.367 --> 00:03:48.767
-Yep.

00:03:48.767 --> 00:03:50.868
-We have an all-military
audience tonight,

00:03:50.868 --> 00:03:52.968
and I wanted to ask you,
is it true that you trained

00:03:52.968 --> 00:03:55.534
with the Royal Marines
for the last World Cup?

00:03:55.534 --> 00:03:58.434
-I did, yes.
So, before the last World Cup,

00:03:58.434 --> 00:04:01.400
our coach took us down
to the Royal Marines.

00:04:01.400 --> 00:04:04.534
And was like, "Yeah, we're gonna
be here for a few days,"

00:04:04.534 --> 00:04:07.467
and kind of get together
and do some team bonding.

00:04:07.467 --> 00:04:09.734
And I loved it, if I'm honest.
I really enjoyed it.

00:04:09.734 --> 00:04:12.534
We kind of --
They took our phones away,

00:04:12.534 --> 00:04:16.400
put us in the uniform,
kind of took us straight out

00:04:16.400 --> 00:04:18.667
to kind of this --
in the middle of a forest,

00:04:18.667 --> 00:04:23.234
and we learned how to kind of
put up the tents they sleep in

00:04:23.234 --> 00:04:26.167
and kind of cooking on the fire.

00:04:26.167 --> 00:04:28.501
-The soccer team?
-Yeah, we was all there

00:04:28.501 --> 00:04:31.300
with the Marines,
and, yeah, was doing that.

00:04:31.300 --> 00:04:32.667
Slept over.
We done some of that

00:04:32.667 --> 00:04:35.400
tactical training in the woods
with some --

00:04:35.400 --> 00:04:39.901
Yeah, and then a three-mile hike
at 5:00 a.m. the next morning.

00:04:39.901 --> 00:04:41.267
We done it all.
-I couldn't do any

00:04:41.267 --> 00:04:43.100
of those things
that you just said.

00:04:43.100 --> 00:04:45.267
I couldn't set up a tent if --
Yeah, no.

00:04:45.267 --> 00:04:46.667
-No, we done it all.
We done kind of

00:04:46.667 --> 00:04:49.801
all the training, the --
I think they called it

00:04:49.801 --> 00:04:52.767
sheep's dip, when you go under
the tunnel in the water

00:04:52.767 --> 00:04:54.400
and everything like that.
-Oh, my gosh.

00:04:54.400 --> 00:04:57.367
-Yeah, it was really cool.

00:04:57.367 --> 00:04:59.667
We was grateful, kind of
that team bonding aspect.

00:04:59.667 --> 00:05:02.400
We were together for three days,
getting to know them.

00:05:02.400 --> 00:05:04.367
They was getting to know us.
As a team, we was together.

00:05:04.367 --> 00:05:06.834
And I think it really helped us
in that World Cup.

00:05:06.834 --> 00:05:08.334
-Right now,
you're four goals away

00:05:08.334 --> 00:05:11.934
from being England's top
goal-scorer of all-time.

00:05:11.934 --> 00:05:14.100
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:14.100 --> 00:05:16.234
I mean, what --
What does that --

00:05:16.234 --> 00:05:19.400
I mean, how are you feeling
going into this --

00:05:19.400 --> 00:05:20.634
this year's World Cup?

00:05:20.634 --> 00:05:21.934
-Yeah, I mean, I'm excited.

00:05:21.934 --> 00:05:24.701
You know, the last World Cup
was really special.

00:05:24.701 --> 00:05:27.067
We got to the semifinal,
which was the first semifinal

00:05:27.067 --> 00:05:29.767
we'd got to in like
30 years as a nation.

00:05:29.767 --> 00:05:31.634
And the country
was going pretty mad.

00:05:31.634 --> 00:05:33.868
But, of course, we fell
that one step short,

00:05:33.868 --> 00:05:35.267
so I'm really looking forward
to this one.

00:05:35.267 --> 00:05:37.434
We have a great team.

00:05:37.434 --> 00:05:38.968
Really good players,
really good coach.

00:05:38.968 --> 00:05:42.000
We've been kind of building
nicely to -- to this World Cup.

00:05:42.000 --> 00:05:43.300
And I'm really
looking forward to it.

00:05:43.300 --> 00:05:44.968
And hopefully, yeah,
can try and break that

00:05:44.968 --> 00:05:46.801
goal record whilst we're there.

00:05:46.801 --> 00:05:49.367
-Wow, Harry Kane.
We -- you know, I was gonna

00:05:49.367 --> 00:05:51.534
challenge you to something,
some type of --

00:05:51.534 --> 00:05:54.067
but you would just
crush me in anything.

00:05:54.067 --> 00:05:56.167
But then I go, "Oh,
this might be a good idea."

00:05:56.167 --> 00:05:59.434
Would you -- Would you like to
play me in a game of foosball?

00:05:59.434 --> 00:06:02.033
-Let's do it.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:02.033 --> 00:06:05.968
-A mini --
a mini foosball table here.

00:06:05.968 --> 00:06:07.434
-Have you been --
Have you been practicing?

00:06:07.434 --> 00:06:09.534
-I have not been practicing, no.
Let me just see what it's like.

00:06:09.534 --> 00:06:11.234
Okay, good.
All right, that's me there.

00:06:11.234 --> 00:06:12.267
Okay, good.

00:06:12.267 --> 00:06:13.834
First one to 2 wins?
Is that okay?

00:06:13.834 --> 00:06:15.300
-Okay, let's do it, yeah.
-All right, buddy.

00:06:15.300 --> 00:06:16.567
Good luck.
No -- No hard feelings, right?

00:06:16.567 --> 00:06:18.634
-All the best, yeah?
-Yeah.

00:06:18.634 --> 00:06:20.901
[ Drumroll ]

00:06:20.901 --> 00:06:23.701
♪♪

00:06:23.701 --> 00:06:25.200
-Oh.

00:06:25.200 --> 00:06:26.868
-Oh. My God.
[ Ding! ]

00:06:26.868 --> 00:06:28.167
[ Cheers and applause ]
You're that fast?

00:06:28.167 --> 00:06:29.267
All right.
1-0.

00:06:29.267 --> 00:06:30.501
-1-nil.

00:06:30.501 --> 00:06:32.267
-That was a good shot.
-Thank you.

00:06:32.267 --> 00:06:33.901
That's a striker, right?
-Yeah, that was a striker.

00:06:33.901 --> 00:06:35.534
Okay, ready?

00:06:35.534 --> 00:06:39.901
♪♪

00:06:39.901 --> 00:06:41.200
Huh! No!
[ Ding! ]

00:06:41.200 --> 00:06:42.801
[ Cheers and applause ]
I did it myself.

00:06:42.801 --> 00:06:44.767
I can't even win at that!

00:06:44.767 --> 00:06:47.267
I can't even win in this game!

00:06:47.267 --> 00:06:49.667
Harry Kane, everybody!
The champ.

00:06:49.667 --> 00:06:52.133
You can watch him compete in
the World Cup later this year.

